  "review": [
    "No chorus. 40 printed lines across 3 stanzas (16/16/8); the source's mid-word line splits in 2:5-2:6 (العار) and 3:7-3:8 (الآلام) are rendered as complete Hebrew words on each printed line, since a line-break maqaf is banned by house style. المسيح → הַמָּשִׁיחַ, صليب → צְּלָב, فدى → פִּדְיוֹן/פּוֹדֶה, سكيب → נֶסֶךְ per glossary. 1:5 \"أنتَ مَنْ أنتَ؟\" kept as a direct question; 2:10-2:12 the love's eternity (أزلي أبدي) is feminine to agree with אַהֲבָתְךָ. No twin in Book 2/3."
